---
import '../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Resources | PGNX</title>
	</head>
	<body class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-b from-white via-green-50 to-white text-gray-900 relative">

		<div
			class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 -z-10"
			style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #16653480 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 24px 24px;"
		></div>

		<div class="pointer-events-none fixed left-1/2 top-40 -z-10 h-[500px] w-[500px] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-green-300 opacity-20 blur-3xl"></div>

		<!-- Top bar -->
		<header class="relative w-full py-6 px-6 flex items-center justify-end">
			<div class="absolute left-0 top-1/2 h-1 w-full -translate-y-1/2 bg-green-800"></div>
			<a href={base} class="relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center gap-1 bg-white rounded-full p-1">
				<img src={`${base}logo.jpg`} alt="PGNX logo" class="h-20 w-20 rounded-full object-cover border border-green-100" />
			</a>
		</header>

		<!-- Side menu toggle tab -->
		<button
			id="menu-toggle"
			class="fixed left-0 top-28 z-40 flex flex-col items-center gap-2 rounded-r-xl bg-green-800 text-white px-2 py-5 [writing-mode:vertical-rl]"
		>
			<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="[writing-mode:horizontal-tb] rotate-90">
				<path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/>
				<path d="M9 22V12h6v10"/>
			</svg>
			HOME
		</button>

		<!-- Slide-out side menu -->
		<nav
			id="side-menu"
			class="fixed left-0 top-0 h-full w-72 -translate-x-full bg-green-900 text-white transition-transform duration-300 z-50 flex flex-col"
		>
			<div class="flex items-center justify-end px-5 py-5">
				<button id="menu-close" class="text-2xl leading-none text-white/80 hover:text-white">&#10005;</button>
			</div>

			<ul class="flex-1 px-2 border-b border-white/15">
				<li class="border-b border-white/15">
					<a href={base} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						Home <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
				<li class="border-b border-white/15">
					<a href={`${base}admission`} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						Admission <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
				<li class="border-b border-white/15">
					<a href={`${base}visa`} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						Visa <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
				<li class="border-b border-white/15">
					<a href={`${base}resources`} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						Resources <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
				<li class="border-b border-white/15">
					<a href={`${base}about`} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						About Us <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href={`${base}contact`} class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide hover:bg-white/5">
						Contact <span class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="h-5 w-px bg-white/25"></span><span class="text-white/60">&raquo;</span></span>
					</a>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<a href={base} class="px-5 py-5 text-white/70 hover:text-white" aria-label="Home">
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
					<path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/>
					<path d="M9 22V12h6v10"/>
				</svg>
			</a>
		</nav>

		<!-- Main content -->
		<main class="px-6 py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
			<a href={base} class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:text-green-900">&larr; Back to Home</a>

			<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-extrabold text-green-800">Resources</h1>
			<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Practical guides for your visa application &mdash; from photo requirements to what to bring on the day.</p>

			<!-- Avoid Corrections Notice -->
			<section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-amber-300 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Avoid Corrections &mdash; Reduce Visa Delays</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					A very high number of corrections is being issued on visa applications these days, and
					it's one of the main causes of appointment delays. When documents are incomplete,
					outdated, or improperly uploaded, the embassy has to issue corrections and re-review
					those cases &mdash; slowing the process down not just for one applicant, but for everyone
					in the queue.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-gray-800">Most corrections come from:</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Blocked account issues (old confirmation, or inactive account)</li>
					<li>Incomplete or unclear admission letters (not full/updated admission)</li>
					<li>Missing IBCC attestation (for Bachelor's students)</li>
					<li>School leaving certificate / Anabin recognition issues</li>
					<li>Incomplete CV &mdash; provide an updated one</li>
					<li>Health insurance not valid or not uploaded properly</li>
					<li>Old travel insurance &mdash; provide one with updated dates</li>
					<li>Resident permit section &mdash; upload your CNIC here</li>
					<li>Passport &mdash; upload all 4 pages, including your signature on page 3</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-gray-800">Before you submit:</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Submit complete and correct documents</li>
					<li>Keep your blocked account updated and valid</li>
					<li>Ensure your admission letter clearly shows full-time enrollment</li>
					<li>Get all academic documents attested (IBCC where required, HEC mandatory)</li>
					<li>Provide valid and clear language proof</li>
					<li>Double-check everything before submission</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">&mdash; PGNX Team</p>
			</section>

			<!-- Biometric Photo Requirements -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Biometric Photo Requirements</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					High-quality photos are essential for facial biometrics in ID documents. If requirements
					aren't met, biometric recognition may not function and the image may not be accepted.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Format</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					The photo must clearly show facial features from the bottom of the chin to the crown
					(top of the head, not the hair), plus both sides of the face. The face must take up
					70&ndash;80% of the photo (32&ndash;36mm in height; rejected only if under 27mm or over 40mm).
					With voluminous hairstyles, the whole head should stay visible without shrinking the
					face. The face must be centred.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Focus, Lighting &amp; Background</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Sharp focus with proper contrast; even lighting with no shadows, reflections, or red
					eyes. Background must be one bright, plain colour (ideally neutral grey) contrasting
					with face and hair &mdash; no patterns, no other people or objects, no shadows on the
					background.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Photo Quality</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Printed on high-quality paper at 600 dpi minimum. Colour photos need accurate skin
					tones. No creases, damage, or staining. Black &amp; white or colour are both acceptable.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Head Position, Eyes &amp; Expression</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Head neither tilted nor turned (portrait style). Neutral expression, mouth closed,
					looking directly at the camera. Eyes open and clearly visible, not covered by hair or
					eyeglass frames.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Glasses &amp; Head Coverings</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Eyes must be clearly visible &mdash; no tinted lenses, no flash reflection off glasses,
					and frames must not cover the eyes. Head coverings are generally not permitted, with
					exceptions for religious reasons &mdash; in that case, the face must remain fully visible
					from chin to forehead with no shadows.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Children &amp; Babies</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					For children aged 9 and under, the face should take up 50&ndash;80% of the photo
					(22&ndash;36mm; rejected only if under 17mm or over 40mm). Children aged 5 and under
					don't need a neutral expression or direct gaze, and don't need to be centred. Babies
					under one year don't need their eyes open.
				</p>

				<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900">
					<strong>Common rejections to avoid:</strong> too close/far, not centred, blurred, too
					dark/light, shadow across face or behind head, busy background, unnatural colour,
					creases, mouth open, head tilted, eyes closed, hair across eyes, looking away, wearing
					a hat, frames covering eyes, dark tinted glasses, flash reflection on glasses.
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Karachi Embassy Checklist -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Appointment Checklist &mdash; Karachi Embassy</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-700">
					<strong>Embassy of the Federal Republic of Germany in Karachi</strong><br />
					92-A/7, Block 5, Clifton, Karachi, Pakistan<br />
					Phone: +92 21 3582 1596 &middot; Email: visa@kara.diplo.de<br />
					<a href="https://pakistan.diplo.de/pk-en/vertretungen/generalkonsulat1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-green-700 underline">Official website</a>
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Bring with you</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Biometric photo (see requirements above)</li>
					<li>Visa fee &mdash; EUR 75 for applicants 18+, paid in cash (local currency)</li>
					<li>Appointment confirmation copy</li>
					<li>Proof of sufficient health insurance for Germany (if not already submitted via the Consular Services Portal)</li>
					<li>Passport (original)</li>
					<li>School-leaving certificate (original)</li>
					<li>Proof of admission to a full-time degree programme (original)</li>
					<li>Proof of secure livelihood (original)</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">You don't need to bring documents already uploaded to the Consular Services Portal.</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Please note</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Arrive 15 minutes before your appointment</li>
					<li>No electronic devices or sharp objects allowed</li>
					<li>A small bag with your application documents is fine</li>
					<li>Arriving late means an automatic cancellation &mdash; you'll need to rebook</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<!-- Islamabad Embassy Checklist -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Appointment Checklist &mdash; Islamabad Embassy</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-700">
					<strong>Embassy of the Federal Republic of Germany in Islamabad</strong><br />
					Ramna 5, Diplomatic Enclave, Islamabad, Pakistan<br />
					Phone: +92 51 2007 200
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Bring with you</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Biometric photo (see requirements above)</li>
					<li>Visa fee &mdash; EUR 75 for applicants 18+, paid in cash at the HBL Bank branch at Ramna 5, Diplomatic Enclave (about a 15-minute walk from the embassy) immediately after your application</li>
					<li>Appointment confirmation copy</li>
					<li>Proof of sufficient health insurance for Germany (if not already submitted via the Consular Services Portal)</li>
					<li>Passport (original)</li>
					<li>Proof of admission to a full-time degree programme (original)</li>
					<li>Proof of language skills &mdash; language certificate (original)</li>
					<li>Proof of secure livelihood (original)</li>
					<li>Residence permit in the country of application (original)</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">You don't need to bring documents already uploaded to the Consular Services Portal.</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Please note</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Arrive 15 minutes before your appointment</li>
					<li>No electronic devices or sharp objects allowed</li>
					<li>A small bag with your application documents is fine</li>
					<li>Access to the Diplomatic Enclave is only possible via the Diplomatic Shuttle from 3rd Avenue, Quaid-e-Azam University Road. This is a private company and prices may change &mdash; contact them beforehand (phone: +92 333 520 5334, email: waqasdss@gmail.com)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>



						<!-- Expense Breakdown -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Expense Breakdown Sheet</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Germany isn't especially expensive by European standards &mdash; food, accommodation,
					clothing, and cultural activities sit just slightly above the EU average. The main costs
					of studying abroad are living costs, tuition fees, semester fees, and health insurance.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">A Month in Germany (~992 EUR)</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Based on a 2023 Deutsche Studentenwerk survey, a typical student's monthly budget breaks
					down roughly as follows:
				</p>
				<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-green-100">
					<table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
						<tbody>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Rent</td><td class="px-4 py-2">425 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-green-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Food</td><td class="px-4 py-2">250 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Clothing</td><td class="px-4 py-2">48 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-green-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Transport (car/public transport)</td><td class="px-4 py-2">49 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Health insurance</td><td class="px-4 py-2">131 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-green-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Telephone / internet / TV-radio fees / postage</td><td class="px-4 py-2">32 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Study materials / equipment</td><td class="px-4 py-2">24 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="border-b border-green-100 bg-green-50/50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Leisure, culture &amp; sport</td><td class="px-4 py-2">33 EUR</td></tr>
							<tr class="bg-green-100"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-green-800">Total</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-green-800">992 EUR</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">
					This is a ballpark figure &mdash; costs can be lower or higher depending on the city and
					lifestyle. Rent typically ranges 290&ndash;560 EUR and is above average in cities like
					Cologne, Munich, Hamburg, Düsseldorf, and Frankfurt.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Proof of Sufficient Funds</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Since 2019, you must prove sufficient financial resources when applying for your visa.
					As of 1 September 2024, this is set at <strong>992 EUR/month or 11,904 EUR/year</strong>.
					This is usually shown via a deposit in a blocked account, or proof of parental income.
					Confirm exact terms with your German embassy or consulate.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Semester Fee</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					All students pay a semester contribution (covering Studentenwerk support services and
					the AStA student body), typically <strong>100&ndash;350 EUR</strong>, paid at registration
					and before each new semester. Some universities bundle in a "semester ticket" for free
					local public transport; others charge it separately (25&ndash;200 EUR).
				</p>
				<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-green-50 border border-green-100 p-4 text-sm text-green-800">
					<strong>Example &mdash; University of Cologne, Winter 2022/23:</strong> Semester ticket
					201.40 EUR + Studentenwerk contribution 90 EUR + AStA 10 EUR + student sport 1.75 EUR +
					faculty councils 2.50 EUR + admin/hardship fund 3.50 EUR = <strong>309.15 EUR total</strong>.
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Tuition Fees</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Public universities generally don't charge tuition for Bachelor's or most Master's
					programs. <strong>Exception:</strong> Baden-Württemberg charges non-EU students 1,500
					EUR/semester (since winter 2017/18) &mdash; doesn't apply to doctoral students, and
					students already enrolled before the fee was introduced are exempt. Certain specialized
					Master's programs and private/online institutions can charge significantly more,
					sometimes over 10,000 EUR/semester. Fee amount does not reflect program quality.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Health Insurance</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					Mandatory for all students, including EU citizens (unless their home country's public
					insurance is valid in Germany). Public health insurance costs roughly
					<strong>110 EUR/month</strong> if you're 30 or under and haven't exceeded 14 semesters
					of study; it rises to at least <strong>166 EUR/month</strong> after that.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Scholarships</h3>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<strong>DAAD</strong> offers scholarships for German and international students at
					every level, and other political, business-linked, or religious foundations offer
					funding too. Scholarships are rarely awarded for an entire program duration or to
					students just starting out &mdash; selection criteria are strict, with no general
					entitlement.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<strong>Erasmus+</strong> supports study or internships abroad for students from EU
					states plus Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway, Turkey, and Macedonia. Internships run
					2 months to a year; study placements run 3&ndash;12 months, with up to 12 months of
					funding per academic stage (Bachelor's, Master's, doctorate). Erasmus+ students are
					exempt from tuition at their host institution. Ask your university's international
					office for details.
				</p>
			</section>


