						<!-- Steps to Visit the German Embassy -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Steps to Visit the German Embassy (Islamabad)</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					A walk-through of what actually happens on your appointment day, from parking to
					leaving the embassy.
				</p>

				<ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-inside">
					<li><strong>Mobile phone &amp; bag:</strong> after parking, go to a waiting room about 2 minutes away, submit your bag and mobile, and get a token. If someone is with you, hand it to them.</li>
					<li><strong>Enter the shuttle service:</strong> security guards will check your appointment email letter and let you in.</li>
					<li><strong>Waiting hall (again):</strong> wait 5&ndash;10 minutes. Shuttle service tickets start being distributed here.</li>
					<li><strong>Token line:</strong> get a token by showing your ID card copy and appointment email copy.</li>
					<li><strong>QR code shuttle ticket:</strong> show your token, pay Rs. 1500, and get a ticket.</li>
					<li><strong>Waiting area (again):</strong> wait in another area; you'll be called after about 2 minutes.</li>
					<li><strong>German Embassy arrival:</strong> board the bus, arriving after 10&ndash;15 minutes; walk about 2 minutes to the embassy gate.</li>
					<li><strong>Embassy:</strong> your name and appointment details are checked against a list. Sit near the front to be called sooner.</li>
					<li><strong>Attendance:</strong> at the next counter, your passport and appointment are checked again.</li>
					<li><strong>Next line:</strong> you'll be sent to another line and called "next."</li>
					<li><strong>Security check:</strong> remove your belt, wallet, and documents and pass through a scanner; items are returned afterward.</li>
					<li><strong>Embassy counters room:</strong> at a table before the 4 counters, pay Rs. 500 for a courier service, give your address and 2 phone numbers, and get a receipt plus your passport back, along with a token (201, 202, 203, etc.).</li>
					<li><strong>Wait for your call:</strong> when your token is called at counter 1 or 2, you'll have your interview with a visa officer, who takes your fee and passport.</li>
					<li><strong>Back to the shuttle terminal:</strong> after the interview, exit and wait for the bus back to where you started; your ticket is collected as you exit.</li>
				</ol>

				<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">
					Note: this account was compiled from the experiences of several community members and
					may vary slightly by appointment day.
				</p>
			</section>

						<!-- Blocked Account via Expatrio -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Steps to Set Up a Blocked Account through Expatrio</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					A full walkthrough of registering with Expatrio, setting up your blocked account and
					health insurance, and transferring your funds.
				</p>

				<ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed list-decimal list-inside">
					<li>Register on Expatrio via <a href="https://www.expatrio.com?p=PAKGERMANNEXUSPGNX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-green-700 underline">this referral link</a>.</li>
					<li>Click <strong>Get Your Value Package</strong>, then <strong>Let's Go</strong>.</li>
					<li>Under "What will you be doing in Germany?" choose the option that fits you (University Student &ndash; Bachelor's/Master's/Studienkolleg/etc.).</li>
					<li>Provide your age.</li>
					<li>For "Are you coming to Germany with dependents who also need insurance?" choose <strong>No</strong>.</li>
					<li>Blocked amount calculation: 992 EUR/month &times; 12 months duration = <strong>12,153 EUR</strong> total to transfer.</li>
					<li>Choose your health insurance plan: <strong>TK (public)</strong> if you're under 30, or <strong>Ottonova (private)</strong> if you're 30 or above.</li>
					<li>Review, tick both checkmarks, and click <strong>Accept and apply now</strong>.</li>
					<li>Provide your email, citizenship, legal name (as on your passport), date and place of birth, phone number, current address, intended university details, and select Pakistan.</li>
					<li>Provide financial details: choose a source of funds (this is a formality &mdash; any option works), repeat it for "where does the money come from," choose <strong>No</strong> for "Are you a US person for tax purposes?", choose <strong>Pakistan</strong> for tax residency, and provide your CNIC as your T.I.N.</li>
					<li>Upload your passport, review the extracted details, tick the checkmark, and continue.</li>
					<li>Review your overall application details.</li>
					<li>Agree to all sections (General, Value Package, Blocked Account, Health Insurance) and submit your application.</li>
					<li>Log in to the user portal (check your email for the password setup link).</li>
					<li>You'll see three sections under review: Blocked Account, Public Health Insurance, and Incoming Insurance. Insurance sections are typically verified within hours; the Blocked Account can take 1&ndash;5 days.</li>
					<li>Once verified, open Public Health Insurance and click <strong>Download</strong> (below Activate). You'll get 4 documents:
						<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside pl-4">
							<li>TK Insurance Certificate</li>
							<li>Incoming Insurance Consultation Protocol</li>
							<li>Incoming Insurance Certificate for Visa Application (EN)</li>
							<li>Incoming Insurance Certificate for Visa Application (DE)</li>
						</ul>
						Merge the 1st, 3rd, and 4th documents into a single PDF to upload in the Health Insurance section on the Consular Services Portal (CSP). Skip the 2nd (Protocol) document. The 1st is your health insurance in both EN/DE; the 3rd and 4th are your travel insurance in EN/DE.
					</li>
					<li>Go to <strong>Home &rarr; Your Products &rarr; Blocked Account</strong> (Awaiting Money Transfer).</li>
					<li>Click <strong>My Payments</strong>, then under Transfers, click <strong>Initiate Payment</strong>.</li>
					<li>For "Where are you transferring money from?" choose <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</li>
					<li>For "How much money do you want to transfer?" enter <strong>12,153</strong> and continue.</li>
					<li>Choose <strong>Someone else</strong> if a blood relative or another person is sending the funds, or <strong>You</strong> if transferring it yourself.</li>
					<li>Provide your sponsor/sender's details, tick the checkmark, and continue.</li>
					<li>On the Summary screen, click <strong>Switch to Manual Bank Transfer</strong>.</li>
					<li>Recheck your details and submit the transfer request.</li>
					<li>Click <strong>Back to your transfers</strong> &mdash; you'll see "Payment 1 &mdash; Transfer Initiated."</li>
					<li>Under Documents, download the <strong>05 Opening Confirmation</strong> document, which contains the German bank and applicant details (double-check these). Take this to your bank so they can transfer the payment to your blocked account.</li>
				</ol>

				<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-green-50 border border-green-100 p-4 text-sm text-green-800">
					<strong>Documents to bring to the bank:</strong>
					<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
						<li>Passport</li>
						<li>CNIC</li>
						<li>Cheque book</li>
						<li>Admission letter</li>
						<li>05 Opening Confirmation document</li>
						<li>Expense Breakdown Sheet (recommended)</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					After the transfer, the bank may take 1&ndash;5 days to complete it. Once your 12,153 EUR
					lands in your blocked account, you can download the <strong>06 Block Account
					Confirmation</strong> document, which you'll upload in the Proof of Secure Livelihood
					section on the CSP.
				</p>
			</section>

						<!-- Visa Interview Questions -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Visa Interview Questions &amp; Sample Answers</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					A community-compiled list of commonly asked visa interview questions with sample
					answers. Use these as a starting point &mdash; always personalize your own answers with
					your real details, and never memorize word-for-word.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Introduction &amp; Background</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Please introduce yourself.</strong><br />I am [Name] from [City]. I completed my bachelor's in [Field] from [University] (CGPA [X]). I've worked/interned with [Company]. I've now been admitted to [University] for a master's in [Course].</p>
					<p><strong>What is the name of your university? Public or private?</strong><br />My university's name is "[Name]" and it is a public university.</p>
					<p><strong>When did you graduate?</strong><br />I graduated in [month, year].</p>
					<p><strong>What was your previous degree, and from where did you complete it?</strong><br />My previous degree is in [field], completed from [university].</p>
					<p><strong>From which university did you complete your last degree, and how was your experience?</strong><br />I did my bachelor's at [university]. My experience was quite good and I learned a lot.</p>
					<p><strong>What was the duration of your previous degree and your CGPA?</strong><br />My previous degree was a [X]-year bachelor's, and my CGPA was [X].</p>
					<p><strong>Where were you born?</strong><br />I was born in [city], Pakistan (see your passport).</p>
					<p><strong>How long did it take you to reach Islamabad?</strong><br />I traveled for [X] hours to reach Islamabad from [city].</p>
					<p><strong>What is your passport number and its expiry date?</strong><br />My passport number is [number], expiring on [date].</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Choosing Germany, the University &amp; the Course</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Why did you choose Germany for your studies?</strong><br />Germany offers free, high-quality education combining theoretical learning with practical training, plus strong career opportunities.</p>
					<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific university?</strong><br />It offers exactly the course I want, has good research facilities, and updated course content.</p>
					<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific course?</strong><br />It's related to my previous qualification and I have a strong interest in this field.</p>
					<p><strong>Is this course relevant to your previous degree? How?</strong><br />Yes &mdash; I studied [3 related subjects] in my previous degree, which form the foundation for this course.</p>
					<p><strong>What will you study in this course?</strong><br />Both theoretical and practical subjects such as [2&ndash;3 subjects], which will build the skills I need in my field.</p>
					<p><strong>Why didn't you apply for English-speaking countries like the UK or Australia?</strong><br />Germany offers high-quality education with no tuition fees and strong job opportunities after graduation.</p>
					<p><strong>Why didn't you apply for this program in Pakistan / at NUST or LUMS?</strong><br />The course content in Pakistan is mostly outdated and theory-focused; German universities emphasize practical learning and industry collaboration.</p>
					<p><strong>Are universities in Pakistan offering the same course?</strong><br />Research facilities in my field aren't sufficient in Pakistan, and there are more job opportunities in Germany.</p>
					<p><strong>Why not pursue a job in Pakistan instead / why studies instead of continuing your job?</strong><br />Growth opportunities and entry-level salaries in Pakistan are limited; I want to build my skills and career through studying in Germany.</p>
					<p><strong>Have you searched for other countries?</strong><br />Yes/No &mdash; I considered [countries] but chose Germany for its tuition-free, high-quality education.</p>
					<p><strong>What developed your interest in studying this course?</strong><br />I studied related courses during my last degree, found them interesting, and decided to specialize further.</p>
					<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific intended program?</strong><br />This field is growing rapidly with strong career demand, and/or it builds on my relevant work experience.</p>
					<p><strong>How does this course align with your previous studies?</strong><br />My previous degree covered subjects closely related to this course's content.</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Sponsorship &amp; Finances</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Who is sponsoring you? What's their source of income?</strong><br />My father is sponsoring me; he is a [profession].</p>
					<p><strong>What are the occupations of your parents?</strong><br />My father is a [profession], and my mother is a [homemaker/profession].</p>
					<p><strong>How much does your sponsor earn per month/year?</strong><br />My sponsor earns approximately [amount] per year.</p>
					<p><strong>Is your father retired or still working? What's his income?</strong><br />My father is still in service, earning [amount] per month.</p>
					<p><strong>What is the blocked account amount you have submitted?</strong><br />I have submitted [11,904/12,153] euros for the blocked account.</p>
					<p><strong>How will you manage your expenses in your 2nd year?</strong><br />I will take up a part-time job, and/or my family will continue supporting me.</p>
					<p><strong>How will you pay your second-semester fee?</strong><br />My second semester fee is nominal (around 300 euros), manageable from savings or part-time work.</p>
					<p><strong>What is your current salary?</strong><br />I currently earn [amount] per month.</p>
					<p><strong>How much salary will you get after this degree?</strong><br />My expected salary in Germany will be around [amount] per year (before tax).</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Family &amp; Personal</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Do you have relatives or friends in Germany or Europe?</strong><br />No, I don't have any relatives or friends there. (Or: mention them honestly if you do.)</p>
					<p><strong>How many siblings do you have? What do they do?</strong><br />We are [X] siblings &mdash; [briefly describe each].</p>
					<p><strong>Do you have any travel history?</strong><br />No, I haven't traveled before. (Or: mention countries visited.)</p>
					<p><strong>What is your occupation, and what does that involve?</strong><br />I am a [profession] &mdash; briefly describe your role.</p>
					<p><strong>Do you have any publications?</strong><br />No, I don't have any publications. (Or: mention the paper/journal.)</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Program, Admission &amp; Course Details</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Are you going for a bachelor's or a master's?</strong><br />I am going to Germany for a [bachelor's/master's] program.</p>
					<p><strong>What is your intended date of travel?</strong><br />My intended date of travel is [date] &mdash; always a few days after your interview date.</p>
					<p><strong>Which degree are you going to pursue in Germany?</strong><br />I will be studying a [Master of Engineering/etc.] in [course] at [university].</p>
					<p><strong>What is your enrollment deadline?</strong><br />My enrollment date is [date] (see your admission letter).</p>
					<p><strong>Can you hand me a copy of your Enrollment Letter?</strong><br />Yes, here it is (always carry extra copies of all documents).</p>
					<p><strong>What was your CGPA in your last degree?</strong><br />My CGPA was [X].</p>
					<p><strong>Your grades were low/average &mdash; how will you manage at a German university?</strong><br />I've learned from that experience and improved my study habits; I'm confident and disciplined now.</p>
					<p><strong>What are your plans after graduation?</strong><br />I plan to [continue research/get a job in Germany/pursue a PhD].</p>
					<p><strong>Have you received acceptance letters from other universities?</strong><br />Yes/No &mdash; explain your reasoning for choosing this one.</p>
					<p><strong>What is the duration of your course?</strong><br />My [bachelor's/master's] course duration is [X] years.</p>
					<p><strong>When will your classes start?</strong><br />My classes will start on [date].</p>
					<p><strong>Why didn't you apply in the previous semester?</strong><br />My documents weren't complete / I had just graduated / the course was only available this semester.</p>
					<p><strong>Have you applied for a study visa before? Any past refusals?</strong><br />No, this is my first application, and I have no previous refusals.</p>
					<p><strong>Where do you see yourself in the next 5 years?</strong><br />Building my career in [field], ideally with a good company, growing my skills.</p>
					<p><strong>What is your expertise? How will it benefit your studies?</strong><br />I have experience in [field]; this course will deepen that expertise for my career growth.</p>
					<p><strong>How will this course benefit you? What will you do after your degree?</strong><br />I'll gain skills in [2&ndash;3 areas] that will help me secure a job in [field], possibly in Germany.</p>
					<p><strong>How did you learn about this specific course/Germany?</strong><br />Through the DAAD website, or from friends/seniors already studying there.</p>
					<p><strong>Will you return to Pakistan after your studies?</strong><br />I plan to gain a few years of work experience in Germany first, then return to Pakistan.</p>
					<p><strong>What are you currently doing?</strong><br />[Working/studying German/recently finished studies].</p>
					<p><strong>Do you have any work experience? How does it relate to your program?</strong><br />Yes/No &mdash; briefly connect your experience to your intended course.</p>
					<p><strong>Will you do a job in Germany if offered?</strong><br />Yes, gladly &mdash; it would help me gain valuable international experience.</p>
					<p><strong>What will you achieve professionally by graduating?</strong><br />This degree opens opportunities in [related fields], helping my career growth.</p>
					<p><strong>Are you learning German? Have you taken a language test?</strong><br />Yes, I've learned basic phrases like Hallo (Hello), Danke (Thanks), Guten Morgen (Good morning).</p>
					<p><strong>Is German required for this course? How will you overcome the language barrier?</strong><br />The course is English-taught, but I'm learning German alongside to adapt to daily life.</p>
					<p><strong>Why not study in an English-speaking country?</strong><br />Germany combines quality, tuition-free education with strong practical and research focus.</p>
					<p><strong>What will be your compulsory/main courses?</strong><br />[List 3&ndash;4 core modules from your program.]</p>
					<p><strong>What will you do if you don't find a job after your studies?</strong><br />I would pursue an internship, using the post-study 18-month job search visa.</p>
					<p><strong>Which company might hire you after this degree?</strong><br />Companies like [relevant employers in your field, e.g., Deutsche Telekom, SAP, Bosch].</p>
					<p><strong>What will you do if your visa is delayed?</strong><br />I would request a "late arrival" approval from my university.</p>
					<p><strong>What skill will you learn in your degree?</strong><br />Practical skills such as [2&ndash;3 relevant tools/techniques].</p>
					<p><strong>Why do you have a study gap in your CV?</strong><br />I was working, learning German, or completing a certification during that time.</p>
					<p><strong>Why should we grant you a visa?</strong><br />I've met all university, embassy, and visa requirements, making me an eligible candidate.</p>
					<p><strong>How did you become interested in this field?</strong><br />I studied related courses previously, found them engaging, and wanted to specialize further.</p>
					<p><strong>What will you do after returning to Pakistan?</strong><br />I'll look for a job related to my field, potentially at [companies].</p>
					<p><strong>You could have learned German in Pakistan &mdash; why didn't you?</strong><br />I have actually started learning German already, and know basic phrases.</p>
					<p><strong>What is the recent research in your field?</strong><br />[Mention a relevant recent research topic or finding in your field.]</p>
					<p><strong>How will this degree help you in the future?</strong><br />It will open opportunities in [related career paths] and sharpen my problem-solving skills.</p>
					<p><strong>What are the main course modules?</strong><br />[List your program's core modules.]</p>
					<p><strong>How will you manage your studies with the language barrier / if grades were average?</strong><br />I'm hardworking, focused, and confident in my ability to adapt.</p>
					<p><strong>Why haven't you attempted IELTS?</strong><br />My medium of instruction was English, so I was admitted based on an English Proficiency Certificate instead.</p>
					<p><strong>Why aren't you completing your bachelor's in Pakistan / going after 2 semesters?</strong><br />I completed the required semesters in Pakistan to meet Germany's 13-years-of-education requirement, since studying in Germany was always my goal.</p>
					<p><strong>To how many universities did you apply? Did you take admission tests?</strong><br />I applied to [X] universities. [Yes/No] regarding admission tests.</p>
					<p><strong>Will you do odd jobs in Germany?</strong><br />No &mdash; I'll look for internships or part-time work related to my field instead.</p>
					<p><strong>Will you change your course or university after going to Germany?</strong><br />No, this is my desired course and I don't plan to change it.</p>
					<p><strong>Did you take the IELTS exam? What was your score?</strong><br />Yes, I scored [X] bands overall. (Or explain your exemption.)</p>
					<p><strong>In which semester did you apply?</strong><br />I applied for the [winter/summer] semester.</p>
					<p><strong>What courses will you study in the first semester?</strong><br />[Name 3 courses from your program's first-semester module.]</p>
					<p><strong>Which particular subjects are you most interested in?</strong><br />I'm especially interested in [2&ndash;3 specific subjects].</p>
					<p><strong>You have other plans &mdash; are you really going for studies?</strong><br />No other plans &mdash; my sole purpose is to study and build my future in Germany.</p>
					<p><strong>How many years do you intend to stay in Germany?</strong><br />Roughly [X] years, accounting for my study duration plus initial work experience.</p>
					<p><strong>What is your backup plan in case of visa refusal?</strong><br />I meet all requirements and hope to be approved, but if refused, I will reapply.</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Accommodation &amp; Practical Matters</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>Where will you stay in Germany? Did you find accommodation?</strong><br />Yes, I've secured a spot in the student dorm. (Or: I've applied to Studentenwerk and am also searching privately.)</p>
					<p><strong>I'm not satisfied with your answer &mdash; explain again.</strong><br />Stay calm, rephrase your point clearly and confidently.</p>
					<p><strong>What have you done in the last year?</strong><br />[Learning German/working/completing a certification.]</p>
					<p><strong>Is studying in Germany easy?</strong><br />It will be challenging but rewarding &mdash; my academic background prepares me well.</p>
				</div>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">General Knowledge About Germany</h3>
				<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					<p><strong>What is the capital of Germany?</strong><br />Berlin.</p>
					<p><strong>Name 5 big cities in Germany.</strong><br />Berlin, Hamburg, Munich, Cologne, and Frankfurt.</p>
					<p><strong>Who is the current Chancellor of Germany?</strong><br />Check the current name before your interview, as this changes over time.</p>
					<p><strong>How many states does Germany have?</strong><br />16 states, including Bavaria, Berlin, Hesse, and Hamburg.</p>
					<p><strong>What is the population of Germany?</strong><br />Around 83 million.</p>
					<p><strong>How many neighboring countries does Germany have? Name a few.</strong><br />9 neighbors, including France, Switzerland, Poland, Austria, and Denmark.</p>
					<p><strong>What's the scope of your field in Germany?</strong><br />[Field] has strong demand in Germany &mdash; mention specific sectors/companies relevant to your subject.</p>
					<p><strong>What improvements will AI bring to your field?</strong><br />[Give a brief, thoughtful answer tailored to your field &mdash; tech, business, healthcare, etc.]</p>
				</div>

				<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-600 italic">Best of luck with your visa interview!</p>
			</section>

						<!-- Release Letter Steps -->
			<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/60 backdrop-blur-sm border border-green-100 shadow-sm p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-800">Steps to Get a Release Letter (Discard Your Application)</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
					If you need to discard your current visa application and get a Release Letter, follow
					this process.
				</p>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Booking the Appointment</h3>
				<ol class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-decimal list-inside">
					<li>Book an appointment at <a href="https://service2.diplo.de/rktermin/extern/appointment_showMonth.do" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-green-700 underline">service2.diplo.de</a>.</li>
					<li>Select the category: <em>&Ouml;ffentliche Beglaubigung von Fotokopien und Unterschriften, Ausstellung von Bescheinigungen</em> (Public notarization of photocopies and signatures; issuance of certificates).</li>
					<li>Book on any available date.</li>
					<li>You'll receive an appointment confirmation email.</li>
				</ol>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">Required Documents</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside">
					<li>Photocopy of Blocked Account Confirmation document</li>
					<li>Blocked Account Transfer document (not required, but recommended)</li>
					<li>3 photocopies of the Appointment Confirmation email</li>
					<li>CNIC original + 2 photocopies</li>
					<li>Passport original + 2 photocopies</li>
				</ul>

				<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-green-800">On Appointment Day</h3>
				<ol class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700 list-decimal list-inside">
					<li>Reach the embassy 1 to 1.5 hours early.</li>
					<li>Go to the waiting area and submit your mobile phone and other items, if any. If you don't have any items, continue inside.</li>
					<li>Go to the Shuttle Service ticket counter.</li>
					<li>Submit a photocopy of your Appointment Confirmation email and CNIC photocopy.</li>
					<li>Pay Rs. 1500 for the shuttle service.</li>
					<li>You'll get a shuttle bus ticket &mdash; don't lose it.</li>
					<li>The shuttle bus will drop you at the German Embassy.</li>
					<li>At the entrance, they'll check your Appointment Confirmation email and passport.</li>
					<li>Enter the room, take a token, and sit in the waiting area.</li>
					<li>When your token is called, go to the counter and submit your passport, Blocked Account Confirmation photocopy, and Appointment Confirmation email photocopy.</li>
					<li>They will issue the Release Letter.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

